{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team","id":1555635,"title":"Is this a good concept for a First Team?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-19T10:01:20-08:00","id":1555635,"title":"Is this a good concept for a First Team?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">First Team</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">First Team</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Sergei Alekseyev aka Grandpa<br /> Trained as one of the Spetsnaz during the twilight years of the Soviet Union, after the collapse he left to seek work as a freelance agent. Pentex took a particular interest in his set of skills. Now he works keeping the \u201cmuties\u201d in line and he doesn\u2019t like it one bit.<br /> <br /> Position: Team Leader<br /> Equipment: ballistic knife, ID card, rank medallion, M-16 assault rifle with three magazines of ammunition, fianchi law-12 shotgun, 27 12-gauge rounds, 9 dragonsbreath rounds, combat/survival knife with a compass in the handle, flak vest, a salary and a stipend<br /> Attributes: strength 5, dexterity 3, stamina 4, charisma 3, manipulation 4, appearance 2, perception 3, intelligence 3, wits 3<br /> Abilities: alertness 3, athletics 3, brawl 2, dodge 2, intimidation 3, subterfuge 3, drive 3, etiquette 3, firearms 4, leadership 3, melee 2, stealth 3, indoctrination 2, survival 4, investigation 4, law 3, linguistics 5, covert culture 2, medicine 1, occult 1, politics 2, science 2<br /> Backgrounds: rank 2 (First Team Sergeant), resources 3, equipment 4<br /> Investments: immunity to the delirium<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Moira Brown aka Twitch<br /> Moira Brown was recruited into project Aeneid after she discovered she had psychic powers. She is particularly paranoid and jumpy.<br /> <br /> Position: Team Psychic and Second in Command</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Breed: Brain Eater<br /> Equipment: ID card, rank medallion, M-16 assault rifle with three magazines of ammunition, tear gas grenade, combat/survival knife with a compass in the handle, flak vest, a salary and a stipend<br /> Attributes: strength 4, dexterity 3, stamina 4, charisma 3, manipulation 2, appearance (alluring) 4, perception 3, intelligence 3, wits 3<br /> Abilities: alertness 2, athletics 3, brawl 2, dodge 2, etiquette 3, firearms 3, leadership 2, melee 2, stealth 3, survival 3, medicine 1, occult 3<br /> Backgrounds: rank 2 (First Team Junior Officer), resources 3, equipment 2<br /> Fomori Powers: brain eating, immunity to the delirium, mind blast, mind rape, nightmare command<br /> Taints: addiction (brain eating; weekly cycle), breed prejudice (4), derangement (delusions of grandeur), physical wasting (+3; mind blast), teledementia, walking bomb<br /> Numina: psychokinesis +3<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bethany Rodriguez aka the Femoid<br /> Beth went to Dr. Veridian's Workout Program and came out feeling different, she went on a rampage but was discovered by Project Illiad.<br /> <br /> Position: Culinary Specialist<br /> Equipment: ID card, rank medallion, M-16 assault rifle with three magazines of ammunition, combat/survival knife with a compass in the handle, flak vest, a salary and a stipend<br /> Attributes: strength 3, dexterity 3, stamina 3, charisma 3, manipulation 2, appearance (sexy) 5, perception 3, intelligence 3, wits 3<br /> Abilities: athletics 2, brawl 2, empathy 1, intimidation 3, subterfuge 2, drive 1, firearms 3, melee 2, stealth 3, survival 3, cooking 4, medicine 1, occult 1<br /> Backgrounds: rank 1, resources 2<br /> Fomori Powers: mega-strength (+3) enhancement, body expansion, immunity to the delirium, regeneration<br /> Taints: derangement (misandry, sadism, homicidal) mental de-evolution (+3; body expansion), walking bomb<br /> <br /> <br /> Rebecca Fillmore aka Gulper<br /> Becky\u2019s life changed after she started eating at O'Tolley's, she got addicted to the stuff and got hungrier and hungrier. Then everything took a turn when one day she was trying to save money because her habit was expensive but got hungry again, she discovered that she could swallow people. After being discovered by Project Illiad she was recruited into a First Team and now she gets to eat as much as she wants.<br /> <br /> Position: Medic<br /> Nature: predator<br /> Demeanor: confidant<br /> Equipment: ID card, rank medallion, M-16 assault rifle with three magazines of ammunition, combat/survival knife with a compass in the handle, flak vest, first-aid kit, a salary and a stipend<br /> Attributes: strength 3, dexterity 3, stamina 3, charisma 2, manipulation 2, appearance 2, perception 3, intelligence 2, wits 2<br /> Abilities: athletics 1, brawl 2, dodge 2, empathy 1, streetwise 1, subterfuge 2, drive 1, firearms 3, melee 2, stealth 3, survival 3, medicine 2, occult 1<br /> Backgrounds: equipment 1, rank 1, resources 2<br /> Fomori Powers: mouth of the wyrm, stomach pumper, immunity to the delirium, frog tongue, spirit ties, garou gift (Gluttony)<br /> Taints: addiction (Pentex food products, mouth of the wyrm; hourly cycle) derangement (pica, phagomania and cannibalism), severe allergy (tulips, lavender and lotus), worms, mental de-evolution (+1; garou gift)<br /> Merits &amp; Flaws: hidden power<br /> <br /> <br /> Jonathan Cayman aka Danger Joe aka Jarhead Joe<br /> Joey was a fomor since childhood because of the Action Bill Tattoos and other products, he was recruited later in life by Pentex after being discovered by Project Illiad. He is an Action Bill super-fan who keeps a shrine in his dorm. He still thinks he'll meet Action Bill some-day.<br /> <br /> Position: Point man<br /> Nature: addict<br /> Demeanor: fanatic<br /> Equipment: Ithaca M-37 shotgun, 18 12-gauge shells, 6 armor-piercing rounds, Action Bill Special Police Badge, ID card, rank medallion, M-16 assault rifle with three magazines of ammunition, combat/survival knife with a compass in the handle, flak vest, a salary and a stipend<br /> Attributes: strength 3, dexterity 3, stamina 3, charisma 1, manipulation 2, appearance 1, perception 3, intelligence 1, wits 1<br /> Abilities: alertness 1, athletics 2, brawl 2, dodge 2, intimidation 3, streetwise 1, subterfuge 2, firearms 3, melee 2, stealth 4, survival 4, medicine 1, occult 1<br /> Backgrounds: equipment/fetish 3, rank 1 (First Team Private), resources 2<br /> Fomori Powers: shadowplay, wall walking, nightmare command, horns, hide of the wyrm (5), immunity to the delirium<br /> Taints: brainwashed, derangement (temperamental, obsession), special diet (picky eater), severe allergy (soap and broccoli), addiction (crack cocaine, daily cycle), walking bomb<br /> Merits &amp; Flaws: deformity<br /> <br /> <br /> Sidney Peters aka Big Smoke<br /> Sid became a Sicklung fomor via the Smoker's Bane program. After discovering that he had only five years left to live he was approached by Project Iliad who promised him a cure for his condition.<br /> <br /> Position: Technician<br /> Equipment: ID card, rank medallion, M-16 assault rifle with three magazines of ammunition, combat/survival knife with a compass in the handle, flak vest, a salary and a stipend<br /> Attributes: strength 3, dexterity 3, stamina 3, charisma 2, manipulation 2, appearance 2, perception 3, intelligence 2, wits 2<br /> Abilities: alertness 1, athletics 1, brawl 2, dodge 2, empathy 1, subterfuge 2, drive 1, firearms 3, melee 2, repair 4, stealth 3, survival 3, medicine 1, occult 1<br /> Backgrounds: equipment/fetish 0, rank 1 (First Team Private), resources 2<br /> Fomori Powers: noxious breath, immunity (airborne toxins), mega-strength (+3), hazardous breath (lethal smoke), immunity to the delirium<br /> Taints: breed prejudice (1), doomed (five years), derangement (temperamental), bane attractor, walking bomb, inner volcano</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  Details 12-01-2025, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T20:07:09-08:00","id":1555660,"title":"","content":"Action Bill fanboy could be a human. Actually, most members of first teams are humans with specific military skills. If you play Shadowrun or Cyberpunk, just imagine a group of sell-outs and add fomori to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T06:45:30-08:00","id":1555683,"title":"","content":"The leader is a human immune to the Delirium and the only human in the group. I made the Fomor obsessed with Action Bill because I just really liked the concepts from the Freak Legion book and the first edition Book of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-20-2025, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T14:37:09-08:00","id":1555689,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's any particular problem with the concepts in question, but I do think there's a lot of issues with them working together as a single team.<br /> <br /> First, from a narrative perspective, these characters seem to have zero reason to be working together. There's no preexisting ties that bind them together, no mutual goals they can put aside their differences to rally around, etc. They're just a bunch of fomori with some combat training that seem to be assigned together in a fashion that doesn't even track with Pentex's logic for such decisions. It's not even a Suicide Squad level of setup since many of these characters are fomori with enough investment in them that putting them in a dysfunctional group that's likely going to be turned into paste on contact with the enemy is the most likely outcome. There's a significant lack of &quot;why&quot; these characters are working together; esp. as fomori tend to be less interested in Pentex or the Wyrm's larger goals. As a basic thing to address: how is a homicidal misandrist supposed to function in a squad that's half men? What on Earth is holding her back from using her abilities to kill the three men as soon as the opportunities arrive (or at least trying and them killing her instead)?<br /> <br /> Second, there's a problem I see a lot in fictional military units (even from professional writers): a poor understanding of how unit cohesion works in regards to individual specialties. If you want to make a First Team feel like a &quot;real&quot; unit, you have to layer specializations on top of existing commonality. Broadly speaking, soldiers don't start as specialists and then get trained to work together, they start as equals, get trained to work together, and then get additional training in specializations once they've demonstrated their ability to work in their assigned units. While it well predates modern video-games, a lot of fictional squads feel like MMORPG raid parties where there's a vast overemphasis on fulfilling a specific role in the unit: healer, tank, DPS, etc. A realistic military squad is going to have much less variation on roles (they work as a unit to shoot at the enemy), and most specialties are applied between firefights.<br /> <br /> The Garou are a bit of an exception to this second issue, but it's actually addressed fairly well on why that's the case: they have a divinely ordained set of roles in their society and that trickles down into their roles in their packs. It also doesn't hurt that every Garou has a massive boost to their base-line combat utility just from being shapeshifters, so even a minimally combat trained Garou can dish out and take punishment well beyond what all but the most intensely trained humans can manage (at least in close quarters). Garou society (and even BSDs for that matter) can shove a member of each Auspice into a pack and expect it to work out at least short term because the common cultural values they're raised with, and the natural consequences of Auspices being a real thing for them lets them move past the generalist-to-specialist training mentality you would need for getting a squad of random fomori to operate as a First Team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T15:35:43-08:00","id":1555691,"title":"","content":"Well, the Freak Legion book goes over how Fomori working for First Teams are rewarded with money and various products. They're also given the false promise of a cure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-21-2025, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T16:21:53-08:00","id":1555693,"title":"","content":"Also, it's pretty obvious why Jarhead Joe is working for Pentex. He thinks he's training to work with Action Bill and the Danger Squad to fight the evil minions of W.O.L.F. which is honestly hilarious and he gets Action Bill merchandise. Becky is working for Pentex to manage her cravings. Sergei wants to get payed and so does everybody else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-21-2025, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T20:33:11-08:00","id":1555701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555691#post1555691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Freak Legion book goes over how Fomori working for First Teams are rewarded with money and various products.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question isn't why they work for Pentex, it's why they work with this particular group of people.<br /> <br /> Being interested in Pentex or the Wyrm's larger goal is relevant only because it gives characters a baseline commonality to work with.<br /> <br /> Greed doesn't do the work very well in this regard, they'd still each look for a group they relate better to, and Pentex itself would want them in a more cohesive group as they're a relatively high investment.<br /> <br /> As is, this group will die quickly in the field without accomplishing nothing significant simply because they won't work well together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T20:47:39-08:00","id":1555705,"title":"","content":"OK, but I brought up a specific example that &quot;get paid&quot; really doesn't address: a character with three derangements, include misandry and homicidal. She enters states where the only thing she can do is try to murder men. And has to constantly work in close proximity with three men who are not good well adjusted people in their own rights. Why would Pentex put her in this squad and not some other unit/non-First Team division where that's not going to be a problem?<br /> <br /> Also, the team has Resource ratings of 1 to 2. That's barely keeping a roof over your head poor, and stable lower class. These are not people living super-spy lifestyles to go with giving up their souls to Pentex's corporate demands. These are people that come home from jobs that require military equipment to do, and still have to struggle to make sure all their bills are paid.<br /> <br /> I'm not questioning why many of them would agree to work for Pentex broadly, or even whether Pentex could divert them into a combat oriented position. I'm questioning how this specific set of individuals was placed in the same unit together. Pentex isn't Stupid Evil. They can read psych reports of their employees, and task them according to their personalities; not just their skill sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T08:10:36-08:00","id":1555725,"title":"","content":"Well, they're living in dorms provided by Pentex and the level of resources is because of their rank. The more they go up in rank the more they get paid. The book says they start with a resources of 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-21-2025, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T10:38:00-08:00","id":1555730,"title":"","content":"Well, I was thinking that maybe Sid and Beth were primarily the ones used for distractions or doing damage. Now that I think about it, they would probably be an Assault Team which would mean they'd get payed more and have better equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T13:53:50-08:00","id":1555737,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm sure there's plenty of First Teams with homicidal members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T13:59:10-08:00","id":1555738,"title":"","content":"The problem is ones that are actively homicidal at each other with nobody capable of controlling them, and nothing motivating them strongly to take their urges out elsewhere. Sure, if this is a one-off squad that Pentex is just trying to get rid of by sending them on an uber-dangerous mission and hoping most of them die before killing the survivors... that's one thing. If this is supposed to last more than a single mission, there needs to be reasons for the group to hold up as a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T14:10:01-08:00","id":1555739,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm pretty sure that they'd take their urges out on the enemy since they're an assault team which means they're sent into places where encounters with the enemy are likely. Also, Pentex never really cared about personal preference when assembling First Teams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-21-2025, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T15:32:58-08:00","id":1555746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555739#post1555739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm pretty sure that they'd take their urges out on the enemy since they're an assault team which means they're sent into places where encounters with the enemy are likely. Also, Pentex never really cared about personal preference when assembling First Teams.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really how any of this works.<br /> <br /> If as an author you don't give then a reason to be best buddies, the reader has no reason to think they're best buddies, or that them being so makes sense.<br /> <br /> You expect an Assault Team to work because the people assembling them know what they're doing. But as an author you <i><b>are</b></i> the people assembling them, it's on you to figure it out.<br /> <br /> And we're not talking mere personal preferences. We're talking people with uncontrollable urges that Pentex <u><b>know</b></u> to have such problems.<br /> <br /> So the question remains: what, if anything at all, prevents the <b><i>PATHOLOGICALLY</i></b> homicidal and misandrist Hulk from killing her male colleagues? What makes a bunch of deranged people who can barely contain their impulses for a couple hours from just turning upon each other? The three women are one obsessive killer and two cannibals, two of the men are prone to violence anyway, and even the one who doesn't have a derangement still don't like the others and has no reason to not kill them when they inevitably become a problem.<br /> <br /> Derangements aren't personality quirks. Those people can't control those urges reliably. They <b>will</b> target each other if nothing explicitly prevents them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T16:37:30-08:00","id":1555747,"title":"","content":"Well, Becky has mouth of the wyrm which can only work on swallowing something the size of a short person or a medium-sized dog, so she prefers to eat midgets and children. Sid has a bomb in him just in case and so does Joe who is brainwashed which makes him loyal. Moira only has to eat brains once a week, so it's manageable as Pentex can send some poor sap to her dorm. Do you want me to put a bomb in Beth and Moira too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-21-2025, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T17:12:38-08:00","id":1555748,"title":"","content":"We're not asking you to do any specific idea. We're pointing out what we see as a serious flaw in using these characters as a squad in a narrative function. You can resolve it however you want to, it's your idea. If you want to go full Suicide Squad with bombs and a Waller type lording over them? That's a way to do it. If you want to reconsider the characters to make them more compatible? Also an option. If you want to put more energy into giving them a shared history and more personal motivations to actually get along? Again, also an option.<br /> <br /> It's just, as it stands right now, this is an obviously non-fuctional First Team. It's fixable, but it's your idea to decide what the best direction to take that fix in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T11:58:16-08:00","id":1555759,"title":"","content":"While I had considered another concept for a First Team made up of a group of Serpent Brother/Son of Typhon hybrids, a Shadowfiend, a Throwback and an Enticer. It didn't feel as interesting as the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T12:17:44-08:00","id":1555760,"title":"","content":"Also, while Joe was temperamental, when he gets angry he typically throws tantrums like a little kid except for when he frenzies. I still don't see what the problem is, Black Spiral Dancers have a chance to Frenzy but Pentex still hires them into First Teams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-22-2025, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T14:16:08-08:00","id":1555767,"title":"","content":"OK, I gave a very specific example of what I see as the larger problem in Beth. You have not addressed, in the slightest, how someone that has three derangements and mental devolution is supposed to avoid murdering half of her squad. The money rationale is even weaker for her than my broader response to that because you put mental devolution on there. When she's Hulking out, she's very open to her derangements, and not going to be thinking at all about getting paid to put up with her teammates.<br /> <br /> You seem to want to do anything but address that (and largely talk about Joe while I don't think I've said anything specifically about him being a problem). Yes, I can point at other things that don't make much sense to me, but I'm trying to focus on stuff that would help you with the problems I see in the idea that you asked for feedback about that aren't just my personal pet peeves (how can someone be allergic to just broccoli, when they'd have to be allergic to the whole <i>Brassica oleracea</i> family of vegetables; not that him hating Brussels sprouts to would be a problem from a concept standpoint).<br /> <br /> Yeah, all Garou can Frenzy... but the Frenzy rules aren't actually that bad and you can play all Garou WtA games without a Frenzy leading to a bunch of friendly fire. If you were suggesting a BSD Cliath with Rage 10, Gnosis 1, and Willpower 3, coupled with one or more Flaws that make Frenzies more likely/worse? Yeah, I'd be saying that's a problem for a First Team too.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I can be clearer with the core problem: you have not provided a &quot;why&quot; for this group to exist on a narrative level. As a reader, with the information provided, they're suspension of disbelief breaking because they make no sense as a cohesive unit. As I said, this can be fixed. It's not a base concept that's unsalvageable to me. But salvaging it to something that I would think would be broadly enjoyable to see in a story is work that I think you should do.<br /> <br /> If you want me to expand on that I can try, but I'm really not sure what else I can say to make this more clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T15:24:59-08:00","id":1555771,"title":"","content":"Well, the mental de-evolution only happens when her body expands, so I guess she would probably only use it when surrounded by enemies, so she would use it after charging into close combat. And as long as she uses it sparingly the side-effects will just be temporary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-22-2025, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T15:59:29-08:00","id":1555774,"title":"","content":"As for the rolls of each of the characters, well, Beth and Sid are good at dealing damage and Joe is good at scouting. Moira can use her psychic abilities to disable opponents, and Becky can do damage with Stomach Pumper, eat small kinfolk with Mouth of the Wyrm or separate enemies by swallowing some of them with the Gluttony Gift at the cost of a temporary loss of intelligence. Now that I think about it, Becky's Gluttony can be used as a means to restrain Beth if she gets out of control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  details 11-22-2025, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T18:34:52-08:00","id":1555778,"title":"","content":"You're still trying to wiggling around minutiae instead of actually engaging with what I said. If you don't want to talk about the fundamental issue of making this a convincing group of characters that work together, than I guess there's no way for me to further address your ask of the quality of this concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T18:45:07-08:00","id":1555779,"title":"","content":"I thought I explained how she can be controlled in both of the two comments. I said Beth should only use Body-Expansion sparingly and only when she's surrounded by enemies since Mental De-evolution is only temporary as long as it's use is limited. Becky could also swallow Beth with Gluttony if she starts attacking the wrong people. You also asked how they could complement each other as a unit so I listed some ways their powers could be used strategically. As for the narrative don't most First Teams start out not knowing each other and learning to work together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-22-2025, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T20:20:01-08:00","id":1555784,"title":"","content":"Telling me about unit-roles is treating these as monster stat blocks, not characters. Fomori are thinking and feeling human beings with a monster fused to them on a spiritual level. They have motivations and desires. They don't just exist to be a combat role.<br /> <br /> Yes, military style units are generally formed from people that are initially strangers, but that's what lots and lots of training before they're deployed is for. I talked about this already.<br /> <br /> If you want to give them that training... work it into the characters. I also mentioned a method of doing so before as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T06:53:53-08:00","id":1555794,"title":"","content":"What was the method of doing so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T07:21:38-08:00","id":1555797,"title":"","content":"If you're asking about a method, a start might be to think of these proposed character-sheets as &quot;characters in a story&quot;. The point is, there's a role they have to play within the story. They aren't just roadblocks for the players' goals. But right now, that's all you've provided... an inanimate object like a roadblock. All these details... But while I'm reading, my thought-process is me just disinterestedly thinking &quot;Okay... Sure... If you say so...&quot; and it all ends in me just thinking &quot;Who cares... it's just a bunch of whatever.&quot;. These are antagonists with no story-hook. I would never use that troop for a game because, honestly, why would I?! They're cardboards, nothing more. And you might say, you gave them a backstory but I look at that and if I encountered anything like that in a movie, I'd call it a &quot;poorly written character&quot;. <br /> <br /> The reason my ultimate response to this &quot;First Team&quot; is &quot;Who cares...&quot; is because there's no hook. <i>There isn't a single interesting story-bit here.</i> They're bad, <i>really </i>bad... and that's pretty much it. That's <i>boring</i>! <br /> <br /> And the reason I'm saying it like this is because people in this thread have offered kind advice to help you - and you've pushed back at every turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T07:39:44-08:00","id":1555798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555784#post1555784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Telling me about unit-roles is treating these as monster stat blocks, not characters. Fomori are thinking and feeling human beings with a monster fused to them on a spiritual level. They have motivations and desires. They don't just exist to be a combat role.<br /> <br /> Yes, military style units are generally formed from people that are initially strangers, but that's what lots and lots of training before they're deployed is for. I talked about this already.<br /> <br /> If you want to give them that training... work it into the characters. I also mentioned a method of doing so before as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you said something about specialization so, Becky specializes in medicine having paramedic level training compared to the others who can only fix broken bones, Moira specializes in the occult and Joe specializes in stealth. Beth has cooking skills so she's basically the cook of the group. I haven't thought of anything for Sid yet maybe he could be the technician? Sergei is the leader so I guess he covers logistics, he is also the driver. As for a goal that unifies them, most of them want a cure for their condition I guess even if it's an empty promise from Pentex they don't know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-23-2025, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T13:52:38-08:00","id":1555807,"title":"","content":"What I said about specialization was to stop focusing on it in your replies to what I'm saying. We want to know more about who these people are and why they do what they do (including functioning as a group <b>emotionally</b> not just because Pentex says so), because that's what's lacking.<br /> <br /> So, a cure? Do all of them want a cure (Sergei doesn't have anything to cure, Joe doesn't seem to perceive himself as 'sick,' and I'm not sure the rest would necessarily think going back to how they were is better besides maybe one)? Do any of them have a reason to believe a cure exists? Further... does that really address what Knightingale said? &quot;Formor duped into their work for Pentex because Pentex is lying to them about being able to cure them,&quot; is a bit shallow for getting past the &quot;boring&quot; issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T15:33:40-08:00","id":1555812,"title":"","content":"To be fair I said most of them want a cure, Joe just goes along because he thinks he's training to join the &quot;Danger Squad&quot; because the Action Bill Special Police Badge told him that. Becky is provided with Pentex food products for her addiction while being promised a cure, Sid was promised a cure and so was Beth. I honestly don't understand why every character needs a connection to each other the example of the Pentex First Team in the first edition book of the Wyrm had unique personal motivations for 4 of them with only the Black Spiral Dancer having a motivation to protect his teammates. But I guess I could add that Joe has a crush on Becky while Becky just pities him.<br /> <br /> That's all I can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-24-2025, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T16:38:56-08:00","id":1555829,"title":"","content":"Have you got any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T18:55:51-08:00","id":1555832,"title":"","content":"I've suggested more shared background elements simply as one possible way to help deepen the &quot;why&quot; of the group; I've also said going more Suicide Squad style is another option too (though even in the Suicide Squad stories, there's generally an idea that the more regular members do develop emotional bonds over their missions; they're not just mindlessly following orders until they do enough missions or finally bite it). The problem is that these are shallow character ideas... to the point where some people feel like these aren't fully characters yet. <br /> <br /> Whatever ideas I might have, I have no clue if you actually care. You haven't responded to any of the vaguer things I've posted with &quot;hey, could you go deeper on that?&quot; or even, &quot;that's the exact opposite of what I want to do here,&quot; so I have an idea of what would help.<br /> <br /> This is your First Team. You haven't given us a context for why you're making them. Is this for a private game you're working on? Trying to build up stuff for a fan supplement to publish in the STV? Just something you're making to practice your antagonist crafting skills? Going back to a word I've used a lot, there's also their narrative purpose. Is this a just a squad that the actual PCs will probably kill in one session without ever learning about them (in which case, yeah... a bunch of our responses are too much detail but I'd then say there's too much detail broadly for some throwaway mooks)? Is this for a Wyrm game where this is the &quot;B squad&quot; to the PC's &quot;A squad&quot; so they'll show up a lot in &quot;downtime&quot; scenes and possibly big missions so the PCs might want to get to know them? Are you aiming to have them be more sympathetic baddies in a standard game where you want to make sure that the players get to reflect on their humanity even as their characters might not initially care about the carnage they wreck on a bunch of people dealt shit hands only to die pointless deaths?<br /> <br /> You're going to get as specific responses as you frame your ask for feedback. If you want more from us that's really going to mean something, you need to give us more to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T19:02:24-08:00","id":1555834,"title":"","content":"Well, I was practicing my villain crafting skills and considering some of the powers I gave some of them they're intended to last a bit longer than most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T19:08:27-08:00","id":1555835,"title":"","content":"I guess the commonality between the group is that most of them started out as ordinary people and were picked up off the street by Pentex. Maybe a common goal they could be given is that they're convinced that the Garou want to send Humanity back to the Stone Age so they think that killing them would be doing Humanity a service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  details 11-24-2025, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T22:16:48-08:00","id":1555839,"title":"","content":"I see here a lot of the difficulties we had with your Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> You're getting better at making character sheets, but you're still struggling with the <i>concept</i> of making characters, for a story. You think of their backstory but you don't seem to understand it's actually important, or to understand their role in the story beyond the stats.<br /> <br /> As far as derangements go, you have to conceptualize just how intense they are. They're about lack of control. They're about engaging a behavior even when it is completely against your best interest, and about <i>not even wanting</i> to not engage them when this is not the case. They're not about a functional person having personality issues, they're about a person <i>not being functional</i>. And here this is your main problem as far as stats go, their stats are otherwise ok.<br /> <br /> But why do they work together as characters? What would they do and why in a movie or book, where you don't need or have stats at all? If you want nameless mooks, they have maybe more background than they need. But if you want villains that will have more spotlight time and relevant interactions, then you have to think what they are when stripped of stats, that's not just a detail, that's <i><b>the most important aspect</b></i> of a villain, as their interactions, motivations and relationships will usually come into play way before the main confrontation.<br /> <br /> Watch an actual live play at youtube or twitch and you isn't likely to see any of a villain stats nor most of their rules-defined actions. While there are things those live plays don't really do like in a common game at our houses, this definitely is an aspect of the game. It is about the story, not just the stats, and stats alone don't tell much and don't make good villains, it's only one aspect of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T11:29:50-08:00","id":1555861,"title":"","content":"All I could think of was Joe having a crush on Becky who just pities him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T12:32:23-08:00","id":1555863,"title":"","content":"OK, so if the broader context is you practicing your skills... that's all the more important for you to push yourself to come up with stuff rather than us fill in ideas for you.<br /> <br /> My personal suggestion would be to take a mental break from thinking about these specific characters or even the WoD itself, and just look at media about horrible people that you find compelling; and examples you don't find compelling too. I know people have mixed feelings about the value of TVTropes broadly, but the Villain Protagonist page is a giant list of things to look at in this regard because anything that qualifies means the badguy(s) have to be interesting enough to be the center of attention for the story. Even if it can be hard to narrow down a bit to works that focus on a group instead of individuals, it can be really useful to get a sense of both what you personally like in villains as characters, and even things that aren't your specific taste but you can still see why they make interesting characters.<br /> <br /> My personal preference is to look at shorter works even if you're thinking about characters that might last a long time in a TTRPG game. If you can articulate what makes Mr. Pink from <i>Reservoir Dogs</i> an interesting character (or why you think he isn't) despite the fact that we know so little about him, you're getting down to the minimalist core of getting a concept into a character effectively to an audience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T16:56:15-08:00","id":1555867,"title":"","content":"If you're asking me to make new Characters I'm not doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T17:15:00-08:00","id":1555868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555835#post1555835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the commonality between the group is that most of them started out as ordinary people and were picked up off the street by Pentex. Maybe a common goal they could be given is that they're convinced that the Garou want to send Humanity back to the Stone Age so they think that killing them would be doing Humanity a service.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally gave a unifying goal. TV Tropes is not giving me any ideas that aren't two-dimensional. And you want a goal that unites a group, but none of the villains on that page have anything relevant to unifying a military unit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-25-2025, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T18:22:09-08:00","id":1555870,"title":"","content":"I didn't ask you to make new characters, if you're engaging in character making as an exercise that is going to happen on its own.<br /> <br /> I asked you to set the current characters aside to engage with some study of existing media to help identify character qualities that help establish more compelling antagonists. If you want to expand your techniques in manipulating perspective in visual arts... you study different ways existing art manipulates perspective to various effects so you can try and incorporate those methods into your growing suite of skills.<br /> <br /> And you stated a unifying goal, yes, but you haven't integrated it into the characters in any meaningful way. Why do these characters care about doing good by the rest of humanity that they'd want to put their skin on the line to kill Garou? Joe is pretty much the only one that has a clear motivation that could hook into a &quot;greater good&quot; group narrative. Becky is the only one of the rest that might have some lingering desire to be a good person, but she's also never going to be part of normal human society again. It's hard to contemplate that a spec-ops soldier turned mercenary hasn't been too consumed by cynicism to believe that his time is well spent fighting for future people. Sid is likewise not long for this world and doesn't seem to have any reason to care if the Garou make life hell for everyone else. Moira and Beth are both presented the most openly adversarial ones that might actually enjoy a civilization collapse if they can figure out how to be in a good spot for their interests when it happens.<br /> <br /> And I didn't cite TVTropes so it could teach you something, I solely (and I thought fairly clearly) cited it for having an extensive list of things you could go learn from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T18:30:49-08:00","id":1555871,"title":"","content":"Well, the only other motivation I can think of is not dying. I'm at the end of my rope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T18:37:20-08:00","id":1555872,"title":"","content":"Just because Sid will die soon does not mean he has to be selfish. I'm also pretty sure nobody wants to live in a world where civilization collapses. Also, Becky still thinks she'll be cured by Pentex. After all she still felt bad about eating kids off the street before Pentex found her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-25-2025, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T22:03:30-08:00","id":1555874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555871#post1555871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the only other motivation I can think of is not dying. I'm at the end of my rope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms suggestion is precisely to not think about this now and go read and watch stuff. It's a good suggestion.<br /> <br /> Sometimes we're overwhelmed by the current work. Our brains are tired of thinking about that even if we're personally still wanting to see it finished. When that happens, it's a good idea to give it a rest.<br /> <br /> You're not under a time constraint, give this a pause and go consume stories. We all do that from time to time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T18:59:06-08:00","id":1555895,"title":"","content":"By the way, I remember now that Sergei is the Sergeant which means he not only leads the Unit he also trains the Unit. So, that means that he doesn't have to have the same goal as them. He's the one that gives them the goal to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-27-2025, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T19:26:37-08:00","id":1555896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555895#post1555895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I remember now that Sergei is the Sergeant which means he is the one that trains and leads the Unit. So, that means that he doesn't have to have the same goal as them. He's the one that gives them the goal to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> He gives them missions, not personal goals. He also don't make them work as a unit just by being there. He may have personal goals that diverge from those of the others, but there must still be some reason for him to work with those fucked-up dangerous freaks and them following his lead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T19:39:09-08:00","id":1555897,"title":"","content":"The Sergeant gives the unit a common goal during training so they can work as a team. In the army the Goal they often have trained into their minds is to defend the country. But in the case with Pentex that isn't necessarily the case. While some units might be motivated by nationalism that won't work with this unit, some of them may want a cure but not all of them so maybe they're given a common enemy. Sergei on the other hand being a mercenary only cares about getting paid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T20:13:38-08:00","id":1555899,"title":"","content":"He can't give them anything if they don't buy it. Again, he won't make them work together just by being there and having a title.<br /> <br /> Also, it still don't answer the question of why they work with each other.<br /> <br /> Taking this lead, Sergei literally don't like them and is a common human in the middle of a bunch of freak mutants with superpowers and dangerous mental instability, a disaster just waiting to happen right next to him. Mercenaries don't usually accept obviously suicidal missions, they want to live and no amount of money is good for the dead. And it isn't even all that money for a mercenary to begin with, not one taking on this kind of danger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-26T20:27:15-08:00","id":1555900,"title":"","content":"A bit of a counterpoint on that: as written Sergei would have to be 56 at the absolute youngest. As a man that's most likely in his young or mid 60s, if he's still working as a unit level officer as a mercenary there's something a bit unusual going on. He should be comfortably asking for back-line work at that age and assuming 30+ years of combat experience. Either he wants to be in the mud (which means worse pay) despite the risks, or his career has been rocky enough that finding better jobs and better pay would be an issue. It's certainly an area that could add some features to the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T07:48:32-08:00","id":1555912,"title":"","content":"Well, because he's in an Assualt Team I changed his resources to 3 earlier in case you didn't notice and in the Freak Legion book it says that most first teams have at least one human to lead them. And the book goes over the Fomori discrimination in detail. My guess is that Sergei at least tries to act friendly around them which is why I added the Indoctrination skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-27-2025, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T01:38:46-08:00","id":1555937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555912#post1555912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, because he's in an Assualt Team I changed his resources to 3 earlier in case you didn't notice and in the Freak Legion book it says that most first teams have at least one human to lead them. And the book goes over the Fomori discrimination in detail. My guess is that Sergei at least tries to act friendly around them which is why I added the Indoctrination skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>For this kind of trouble, someone of his experience, I'd expect at least Resources 4. But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, you can also use the &quot;low&quot; income to build a story upon. <br /> <br /> The point we're raising isn't if a human is a good addition or if Sergei would act friendly or not. It is, again, what makes Sergei as a person to decide to be there at all. You can have as many human members as you want in as many First Teams as you want, but there must be a reason for those people to be there, a story, motivations, that take into account not only what they mean to the team, but what working to the team means to them.<br /> <br /> We'll always circle back to the problem of those people having no apparent reason to work together at all. This isn't about the Team as a concept having them, is about them as people deciding to be there with those other, particular, people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-28T09:10:28-08:00","id":1555941,"title":"","content":"Maybe, Sergei is working for Pentex because he has a negative reputation due to lacking restraint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-28-2025, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T17:00:26-08:00","id":1555964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555941#post1555941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, Sergei is working for Pentex because he has a negative reputation due to lacking restraint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would only make things worse and not address the points made.<br /> <br /> It doesn't tell why he doesn't see an alternative to working as mercenary, much less for Pentex, it still doesn't explain why he accepts to work with this particular group, it doesn't tell why Pentex has him working with them, much less why they put him in this group.<br /> <br /> And it worsens all the problems already posited, as instead of being at least partially functional he becomes another short fuse in a band of short fuses with nothing to hold them back. This team wouldn't die at their first mission, they'd die before even getting there as they implode in inner violence and at least half the team dies at the hands of their companions.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that mercenaries are already known for lacking restraint IRL, and are even worse in WoD. The kind of person that leaves the military only to become professional fighters is already quite unbalanced. One of them being reviled by other mercenaries for lack of restraint, this person is just as deranged and vicious as a BSD, but without religious zeal to give them purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T17:36:57-08:00","id":1555966,"title":"","content":"He's working for Pentex because he's too infamous to work in many other places. Pentex Assault Teams are stated in the book to be made up of the nastiest guys they have and discipline is severe. Pentex was also stated to hire Mercenaries for their First Teams along with Fomori, Corrupt Mages like Nephandi, Sabbat Vampires and Black Spiral Dancers, so crazy is something they work with a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-29-2025, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-29T22:11:06-08:00","id":1555970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555966#post1555966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's working for Pentex because he's too infamous to work in many other places. Pentex Assault Teams are stated in the book to be made up of the nastiest guys they have and discipline is severe. Pentex was also stated to hire Mercenaries for their First Teams along with Fomori, Corrupt Mages like Nephandi, Sabbat Vampires and Black Spiral Dancers, so crazy is something they work with a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still not answering why those characters are here, just that Pentex would accept them.<br /> <br /> And working with crazy is different from investing in building a team without making this team work. That's going from crazy to stupid.<br /> <br /> You can have Sergei be a psychotic murder-hobo that's perfectly whiling to work for no pay at all as long as he has access to the weapons he wants and the opportunity to kill people, even if this is not an actual derangement on the sheet. That's crazy <b>AND</b> a reason to work for Pentex as merch in a high-risk, low-pay job.<br /> <br /> Not once we said their derangements are a problem. We said their derangements don't work together. Everyone is a single step from murdering everything around them and no one is able to stop them. We also said their self-destructive tendencies aren't a problem, the problem is to have such group get so much investment from Pentex and be expected to last in play, when they're actually likely to explode in extreme violence and go down in a blaze of glory fighting everything up to and including each other.<br /> <br /> If you want Sergei to be able to control this unstable team, he must be capable at deescalation, not at escalating them even further. And he needs to be someone the others follow because they trust, not someone they trust because they follow. And again, why he's here? Why he didn't try to do something else? Not everyone in the world asks or knows your reputation as a merch, why isn't he retired? Why did he accept to lead unstable freaks he don't even like and he very well knows will end badly soon?<br /> <br /> Do not take those questions, or any of the questions we posited at this thread, as saying that this doesn't work. The point is to answer those questions with stories. There are infinite ways for them to be answered, even without changing anything in their stats, as long as you tell a story of how it happened. Maybe try your hand at writing with a short story about them, even if with the team as it is now, just so you get the handle of how they work and what you can do about them, what you <b>want</b> to do about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T07:06:24-08:00","id":1555977,"title":"","content":"Well, the M-16 Assault Rifles, Flak Vests and combat knives are standard issue. Beth's Misandry is a dislike or contempt of Men not an open hostility towards them. I'm also pretty sure there's people who are homicidal, pedophiles or cannibals on the Pentex Board of Directors but they are able to control themselves enough to do business while indulging their darker impulses behind closed doors. And by a lack of restraint I meant that Sergei tends to make a mess after completing an objective, he can stay calm when he needs to be. So, I think it can be manageable.<br /> <br /> The reason they were chosen to work as a team is because their powers would work well against Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-30-2025, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T12:04:30-08:00","id":1555987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555977#post1555977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the M-16 Assault Rifles, Flak Vests and combat knives are standard issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should I take that as meaning Pentex do not really expect them to survive their next mission? Are they expendable?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555977#post1555977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beth's Misandry is a dislike or contempt of Men not an open hostility towards them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing about Derangements.<br /> <br /> They are not personality traits or opinions, they're Flaws with attached mechanics that really hinder the character's ability to function.<br /> <br /> A person may be misandric, homicidal, a pedophile or cannibal and yet have none of those marked as traits in their character sheet. Those work as you're describing.<br /> <br /> Characters with Derangements must roll Willpower in relevant contexts to avoid acting their derangements. Failing a roll means acting immediately and against any personal belief or interest. <b>They are not able to reliably control themselves, period</b>, and will lose their shit sooner or later.<br /> <br /> So if this is a Derangement, she <b>IS</b> openly hostile to men no matter what you say. Depending on edition, she has at best to roll Willpower to avoid being hostile to men under any kind of stress even if she really doesn't want to, on some editions she can't even roll for that. This compounds with Sadistic and Homicidal, as they're also Derangements, she has at best to roll to avoid killing and torturing when she shouldn't, at worse she doesn't even get that and must completely avoid situations where her Derangements trigger. She'll definitely target friends whenever she doesn't have any other valid victim, and given the combination itself she'll definitely have a tendency to go nuts on men at each and every opportunity.<br /> <br /> You're ignoring what Taints and Derangements are in the game. They are meant to make life difficult for the PC by hijacking agency or giving clear and direct disadvantages that can't be ignored. Most Board Directors in Pentex <b>do not</b> have do many Derangements to begin with, especially if it makes them hard to work with, and those who do get away with problems because they're the fucking Board of Directors, they're both rich, powerful, and well protected against each other. What flies for them doesn't for a thug on the streets.<br /> <br /> In real play Beth would be the kind of person who's constantly on edge at the mere presence of males and frequently get arrested for scuffles with men if her team don't actively keep her away from them, the kind who'll not just seek opportunities to kill, but who'll frequently do so without thinking if left alone with anyone at all, especially a man, and who even to fellow women and teammates causes pain all the time in one way or another, a person who must be watched by her own friends all the time or she'll try to kill or maim them at night, and who'll constantly rage against men she has to be near at in her own team, just due to her Derangements, regardless of whatever personality you give her, the rules and the dice will do that.<br /> <br /> Moira doesn't simply casually thinks she's superior, she'll enter full blown delusion at a moment's notice, plan ahead based on an imaginary destiny and act upon those plans. Rebecca literally can't stop eating if her life depends on it, constantly gulping on anything she can put on her mouth (regardless if she should, by the way), to the point that she can eat her own equipment if there's nothing else to eat, and who'll drool at the smell of human flesh in the best situations, again due to a combination that makes her cannibalism even harder to control, what's even worse being the team medic as she'll be exposed to the sweet juices of a human body regularly, and it'll be her own team mates.<br /> <br /> Johnathan and Sidney at least are only <i>extremely</i> prone to bad moods they'll act upon without regard for consequences, but they would still need someone who can manage their impulses when they get in the way of the team, and won't be friendlier with actual friends than they are with everyone else. And absolutely no fucking one in this team can help them as it is now. They barely can help their own Derangements, much less those of their fellow team mates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555977#post1555977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also pretty sure there's people who are homicidal, pedophiles or cannibals on the Pentex Board of Directors but they are able to control themselves enough to do business</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are the ones without Derangements. Those who have... no, they're not. Whenever there are members with Derangements in a meeting, those have to be accommodated, the director in question isn't expected to self-control because that's not a thing.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555977#post1555977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And by a lack of restraint I meant that Sergei tends to make a mess after completing an objective, he can stay calm when he needs to be. So, I think it can be manageable.</div> </div> </div> </div>For him, yes, as this is not a Derangement. But that still leaves in the air how he manage to manage the impulses of people he doesn't even like, or why he would bother instead of just letting them kill each other and ask for a new, more manageable team. As is he can just complete missions by throwing the team at the problem and killing survivor enemies from a distance, then return with the bodies of his charges and get a new batch of freaks.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555977#post1555977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason they were chosen to work as a team is because their powers would work well against Garou.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That alone can be said of plenty Fomors and only talks about their individual prowess (and make it seems Pentex wants them to survive as they're useful). It still doesn't explain why any of them is with this particular team when they could be with any other team best suited for them.<br /> <br /> First Teams and Wyrm Minions in general are prone to Derangements, but that doesn't mean they can control themselves in a team, it means they form teams where their particular problems aren't so internally disruptive. A misandric in a team women-only, megalomaniacs who either lead the team to do crazy stuff or have leaders that can manage their delusions in some way, anger issues in a team where everyone can take punishment and recover no problem with a lot of resilience and a some regeneration (that's what many BSDs do), you can have an all-crazy team as long as their Derangements are things they don't really have to control in the team.<br /> <br /> Wyrm minions with too many Derangements or too unstable combinations aren't long for this world, this is also a very common thing in the setting. Pentex may assemble First Teams on the fly with little regard for how they fit, but when they do so they don't expect those teams to come back alive with any regularity. Teams that last more than one or two missions are those who got lucky and ended up in a good combination to begin with, but as the person telling the story it is on you to devise how this team will survive if <b>you</b> want them to, even if Pentex didn't.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T14:53:08-08:00","id":1556002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555977#post1555977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason they were chosen to work as a team is because their powers would work well against Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so, on a straight mechanical level... what makes you think this? Only one of them has a defensive power to help tank a hit from even a low Rank Garou, and mundane armor is puny in the WoD. Very few of them have high stats to put military grade weaponry to maximal use, or the skills to do a group ambush against creatures with as many perception boosting powers as the Garou have.<br /> <br /> The most likely result of a stand-up fight between this squad and a pack of starting level Garou is that the Garou all take on combat forms, win initiative, and kill most of this squad before they can do anything at all. Even if the Garou's dice good poorly and they're just severely wounding enemies instead of killing them, most of them have low dice-pools so -2 from wound penalties is going to be a big deal for them to counter attack. That's even before something like Jam Weapon or other Rank 1 Gifts that could completely nullify a lot of that this group brings to the table.<br /> <br /> Pentex tends to treat fomori as disposable shock troops against the Garou because it's very hard to make a fomor that's strong enough to pose a threat to the Garou, and overwhelming them with numbers is more efficient. After that, the mind-whammy fomori powers tend to be a bigger threat than straight up combat because that's attacking the Garou where they're weaker, rather than where they're at their strongest; and that doesn't really work with an assault team basis for the unit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-30T17:17:26-08:00","id":1556013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1555987#post1555987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I take that as meaning Pentex do not really expect them to survive their next mission? Are they expendable?<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's the thing about Derangements.<br /> <br /> They are not personality traits or opinions, they're Flaws with attached mechanics that really hinder the character's ability to function.<br /> <br /> A person may be misandric, homicidal, a pedophile or cannibal and yet have none of those marked as traits in their character sheet. Those work as you're describing.<br /> <br /> Characters with Derangements must roll Willpower in relevant contexts to avoid acting their derangements. Failing a roll means acting immediately and against any personal belief or interest. <b>They are not able to reliably control themselves, period</b>, and will lose their shit sooner or later.<br /> <br /> So if this is a Derangement, she <b>IS</b> openly hostile to men no matter what you say. Depending on edition, she has at best to roll Willpower to avoid being hostile to men under any kind of stress even if she really doesn't want to, on some editions she can't even roll for that. This compounds with Sadistic and Homicidal, as they're also Derangements, she has at best to roll to avoid killing and torturing when she shouldn't, at worse she doesn't even get that and must completely avoid situations where her Derangements trigger. She'll definitely target friends whenever she doesn't have any other valid victim, and given the combination itself she'll definitely have a tendency to go nuts on men at each and every opportunity.<br /> <br /> You're ignoring what Taints and Derangements are in the game. They are meant to make life difficult for the PC by hijacking agency or giving clear and direct disadvantages that can't be ignored. Most Board Directors in Pentex <b>do not</b> have do many Derangements to begin with, especially if it makes them hard to work with, and those who do get away with problems because they're the fucking Board of Directors, they're both rich, powerful, and well protected against each other. What flies for them doesn't for a thug on the streets.<br /> <br /> In real play Beth would be the kind of person who's constantly on edge at the mere presence of males and frequently get arrested for scuffles with men if her team don't actively keep her away from them, the kind who'll not just seek opportunities to kill, but who'll frequently do so without thinking if left alone with anyone at all, especially a man, and who even to fellow women and teammates causes pain all the time in one way or another, a person who must be watched by her own friends all the time or she'll try to kill or maim them at night, and who'll constantly rage against men she has to be near at in her own team, just due to her Derangements, regardless of whatever personality you give her, the rules and the dice will do that.<br /> <br /> Moira doesn't simply casually thinks she's superior, she'll enter full blown delusion at a moment's notice, plan ahead based on an imaginary destiny and act upon those plans. Rebecca literally can't stop eating if her life depends on it, constantly gulping on anything she can put on her mouth (regardless if she should, by the way), to the point that she can eat her own equipment if there's nothing else to eat, and who'll drool at the smell of human flesh in the best situations, again due to a combination that makes her cannibalism even harder to control, what's even worse being the team medic as she'll be exposed to the sweet juices of a human body regularly, and it'll be her own team mates.<br /> <br /> Johnathan and Sidney at least are only <i>extremely</i> prone to bad moods they'll act upon without regard for consequences, but they would still need someone who can manage their impulses when they get in the way of the team, and won't be friendlier with actual friends than they are with everyone else. And absolutely no fucking one in this team can help them as it is now. They barely can help their own Derangements, much less those of their fellow team mates.<br /> <br /> <br /> Those are the ones without Derangements. Those who have... no, they're not. Whenever there are members with Derangements in a meeting, those have to be accommodated, the director in question isn't expected to self-control because that's not a thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> For him, yes, as this is not a Derangement. But that still leaves in the air how he manage to manage the impulses of people he doesn't even like, or why he would bother instead of just letting them kill each other and ask for a new, more manageable team. As is he can just complete missions by throwing the team at the problem and killing survivor enemies from a distance, then return with the bodies of his charges and get a new batch of freaks.<br /> <br /> <br /> That alone can be said of plenty Fomors and only talks about their individual prowess (and make it seems Pentex wants them to survive as they're useful). It still doesn't explain why any of them is with this particular team when they could be with any other team best suited for them.<br /> <br /> First Teams and Wyrm Minions in general are prone to Derangements, but that doesn't mean they can control themselves in a team, it means they form teams where their particular problems aren't so internally disruptive. A misandric in a team women-only, megalomaniacs who either lead the team to do crazy stuff or have leaders that can manage their delusions in some way, anger issues in a team where everyone can take punishment and recover no problem with a lot of resilience and a some regeneration (that's what many BSDs do), you can have an all-crazy team as long as their Derangements are things they don't really have to control in the team.<br /> <br /> Wyrm minions with too many Derangements or too unstable combinations aren't long for this world, this is also a very common thing in the setting. Pentex may assemble First Teams on the fly with little regard for how they fit, but when they do so they don't expect those teams to come back alive with any regularity. Teams that last more than one or two missions are those who got lucky and ended up in a good combination to begin with, but as the person telling the story it is on you to devise how this team will survive if <b>you</b> want them to, even if Pentex didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Freak Legion book only said to roll for the Temperamental derangement. Nowhere did it say that you had to make a roll for the Homicidal derangement or Amnesia. So, I'm pretty sure it's a roleplay element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-30-2025, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T11:20:55-08:00","id":1556065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1556002#post1556002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, so, on a straight mechanical level... what makes you think this? Only one of them has a defensive power to help tank a hit from even a low Rank Garou, and mundane armor is puny in the WoD. Very few of them have high stats to put military grade weaponry to maximal use, or the skills to do a group ambush against creatures with as many perception boosting powers as the Garou have.<br /> <br /> The most likely result of a stand-up fight between this squad and a pack of starting level Garou is that the Garou all take on combat forms, win initiative, and kill most of this squad before they can do anything at all. Even if the Garou's dice good poorly and they're just severely wounding enemies instead of killing them, most of them have low dice-pools so -2 from wound penalties is going to be a big deal for them to counter attack. That's even before something like Jam Weapon or other Rank 1 Gifts that could completely nullify a lot of that this group brings to the table.<br /> <br /> Pentex tends to treat fomori as disposable shock troops against the Garou because it's very hard to make a fomor that's strong enough to pose a threat to the Garou, and overwhelming them with numbers is more efficient. After that, the mind-whammy fomori powers tend to be a bigger threat than straight up combat because that's attacking the Garou where they're weaker, rather than where they're at their strongest; and that doesn't really work with an assault team basis for the unit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gift Gluttony can be used to swallow an entire pack of Garou, Body Expansion is good for offense and so is Hazardous Breath and Stomach Pumper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T13:45:28-08:00","id":1556066,"title":"","content":"She has 2 dice on a diff 8 roll that will likely require more than one success (and can be resisted with Dex + Dodge [or Athletics in W20]) for Gluttony.<br /> <br /> And all of that is offense that doesn't really match how much damage Garou can take. None of that addresses their complete lack of defensive powers considering that the Garou are highly likely to go first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-01T21:13:10-08:00","id":1556081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555635-is-this-a-good-concept-for-a-first-team?p=1556013#post1556013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Freak Legion book only said to roll for the Temperamental derangement. Nowhere did it say that you had to make a roll for the Homicidal derangement or Amnesia. So, I'm pretty sure it's a roleplay element.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm pretty sure it's not, because <i>Freak Legion </i>didn't invent Derangements, they're one of the oldest mechanics in WoD as they're literally in the first core Vampire book, and they have been repeated several times across most if not all lines.<br /> <br /> When Derangements don't have stated rolls it's because you can't roll, it just happens.<br /> <br /> Either <i>Freak Legion</i> said that somewhere or it was so badly written that it left the rules out by accident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}